In our view, the question is not the existing NR use of UE autonomous interruption, but how its impact is bounded if it is used in more cases in 6G. It should be noted that such UE specific interruption is not an unrestricted interruption. Taking the collision case in Figure 1 as an example, UE doesn’t create interruptions at new positions, since the interruption is caused by the RF switching for the configured gap-less inter-frequency measurement, and therefore it remains associated with the configured measurement occasions (SMTC) of that layer, in the same way as in NR, e.g., for deactivated SCC measurement, UE is “only allowed to cause interruptions on PCell or activated SCell(s) immediately before and immediately after an SMTC” (TS 38.133 clause 8.2.2.2.3). When UE cannot perform all intra- and inter-frequency measurements in the same occasion, UE only decides which of the configured occasions are used for which layer. Thus, network can still rely on the following information:
Candidate interruption positions: adjacent to the configured SMTC occasions of the inter-frequency layer, i.e., the interruption doesn’t occur away from these configured occasions;
Maximum length of each interruption;
Maximum interruption ratio over time: since UE only uses a subset of the configured occasions for the inter-frequency layer, the number of interruptions doesn’t exceed that of the fully visible interruption case;
Existing exclusion rules: e.g., no interruption during DRX ON duration when no SMTC occasion occurs around it (TS 38.133 clause 8.2.2.2.19).

Also, S1-O1 is not intended for general and unconditional RRM measurements. In our view, the applicability of S1-O1 is bounded by the following conditions:
UE indication: UE indicates that it supports or needs gap-less measurement with interruption for the target layer, e.g., per-MO or per-band indication based on the current serving cell(s) (see sections 2.2 and 2.3), similar to NeedForInterruptionInfoNR-r18 in NR (TS 38.133 clause 8.2.2.2.19);
Network control: as agreed in RAN4#119, “After receiving UE reported gap related capability or other indication, the MG configuration, including gap-less measurement, should be explicitly under network control”, i.e., network decides for each target measurement whether to configure MG, a network configured pattern (S2-O1), or gap-less measurement with UE autonomous interruption, and S1-O1 is network-authorized per measurement configuration;
Quantitative bounds: a maximum interruption ratio, with NR as the starting point, and a maximum length of each interruption, for each applicable scenario.
